module

public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Homology.DerivedCategory.BoundedBelowSerreImage
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.CompactGeneration.SupportedQuasiCoherent
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.KoszulOrthogonality.AffineComparison
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Duality.KoszulOrthogonality.OpenImmersion

/-!
# The structure sheaf generates `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A})`

[Stacks, Tag 09IS] asserts that for a quasi-compact quasi-separated scheme `X` the category
`D_QCoh(𝒪_X)` is generated by a single perfect object, and its proof runs the induction principle
[Stacks, Tag 08DR] over the quasi-compact opens of `X` with the affine case as the base. This file
proves that base case: for a commutative ring `A`, an object of `D(𝒪_{Spec A})` with
quasi-coherent cohomology sheaves which receives only zero morphisms from the shifts of
`𝒪_{Spec A}[0]` is zero.

It is the Koszul detection statement of [Stacks, Tag 09IR] for the **empty** sequence. For
`f₁, …, f_r ∈ A` the statement `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero`
detects the zero object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A})` from two hypotheses: vanishing of the morphisms out
of the shifts of the sheafified Koszul complex, and vanishing of the restriction to
`U = D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r)`. For `r = 0` the open `U` is empty, so the second hypothesis carries no
information and can be dropped — the proof uses it only to produce the `f_i`-power torsion of the
cohomology modules, and there are no `f_i`. What remains is exactly the base case of
[Stacks, Tag 09IS]: the Koszul complex of the empty sequence is `𝒪_{Spec A}` in degree zero.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Duality.Affine.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_empty_eq_zero` — the detection
  statement of `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero` for the empty
  sequence, with the hypothesis on the restriction dropped rather than discharged.
* `Stacks.Duality.Affine.koszulObjectEmptyIso` — the Koszul object of the empty sequence is
  `𝒪_{Spec A}` placed in degree zero.
* `Stacks.Duality.Affine.isZero_of_forall_hom_structureSheaf_eq_zero` — **the affine case of
  [Stacks, Tag 09IS]**, in the ambient derived category: an object of `D(𝒪_{Spec A})` with
  quasi-coherent cohomology sheaves and no nonzero morphism out of a shift of `𝒪_{Spec A}[0]` is
  zero.
* `Stacks.Duality.Affine.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_structureSheaf` — the same read as
  `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator` for the one-object family
  `{𝒪_{Spec A}[0]}` inside `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A})`, which is the shape the induction step
  `Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_openImmersion` consumes.

## Implementation notes

**No `@[stacks 09IS]` attribute is attached here.** Tag 09IS is a statement about a quasi-compact
quasi-separated scheme, and asserts in addition that the generator is a *perfect* object; what is
proved here is its affine case, and only the generation half of it. The tag is registered in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedQCoh/PerfectGeneratorInduction.lean`, on
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.hasPerfectGenerator_of_qcqs` and on
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.exists_isPerfect_isZero_iff_forall_hom_eq_zero`. Its other inputs
are the induction principle [Stacks, Tag 08DR], which the library has as
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.InductionPrinciple.induction_isCompact_open` and `induction_top`, the
inductive step, which the library has as
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection_of_prop`
(`…/DerivedQCoh/AnyModel/GenerationStepOnASubcategory.lean`) — and equivalently as
`…isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_openImmersion` together with
`Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isIso_unit_of_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero`
(`…/Duality/KoszulOrthogonality/AffineSituation.lean`, registered for 09IR,
implication (2) to (1)) for its
hypothesis `hunit` — and the extension of a perfect object from a quasi-compact open,
[Stacks, Tag 09IQ].

The inductive step is not
`…isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_detection`, and the library has 09IQ beyond the
affine case. The `_of_detection` form quantifies its hypothesis `hdet` over all of
`D(𝒪_Y)`, and the docstring of
`Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isIso_unit_iff_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero` records in its own words that
"`hdet` as stated here is false, and this statement is therefore vacuous", with a
discrete-valuation-ring counterexample; so the `_of_openImmersion` form with 09IR is the pair to
use. And 09IQ is proved unconditionally at a quasi-compact open of a quasi-compact
quasi-separated scheme, at the locally small model, as
`Stacks.DerivedQCoh.AnyModel.exists_isPerfect_retract_derivedRestrict` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/DerivedQCoh/AnyModel/PerfectSummandOfRestriction.lean`; its input
[Stacks, Tag 09IM] is proved for a general closed `T` with retrocompact complement as
`Stacks.Perfect.LiftingComplexes.exists_isPerfect_lift`, and [Stacks, Tag 08EK],
[Stacks, Tag 08EH] and [Stacks, Tag 08DD] are all registered as well. What is left of 09IS is the
induction itself and the perfection of the generator.

**The model is the locally small one.** No `HasDerivedCategory` binder appears below, so the
global instances of `StacksFrontier/Homology/DerivedCategory/LocallySmall.lean` are in force. This is
forced rather than chosen: the proof passes through the affine derived Spec–Γ equivalence of
[Stacks, Tag 06Z0], which is available at that model and no other, and it is also the only model
at which [Stacks, Tag 09IS] has content — see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Duality/CompactGeneration.lean`.

**The generator is written `𝒪_{Spec A} = (A)^~`.** The structure sheaf is spelled
`(AlgebraicGeometry.tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A)).obj (ModuleCat.of A A)` rather than
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.unit (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf`, which
`AlgebraicGeometry.tildeSelf` identifies with it by `Iso.refl`. The first spelling is the one the
Koszul object produces and the one for which instance synthesis finds the quasi-coherence
instance; see the implementation notes of
`StacksFrontier/Homology/PseudoCoherentRelative/TildeFiniteFree.lean` for the synthesis failure the
second spelling causes.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 09IQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09IQ)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 08DR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/08DR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06Z0](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06Z0)
-/

-- This file uses the locally small derived-category models below, which are not
-- global instances (see `StacksFrontier.Homology.DerivedCategory.LocallySmall`):
-- `D(R)` for `R`-modules.
-- `D(R)` for sheaves of modules on a small site.
-- `D(𝒪_X)` for a scheme.
attribute [local instance] ModuleCat.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] SheafOfModules.hasDerivedCategory
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.hasDerivedCategory

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty
open CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated

universe u

namespace Stacks.Duality

/-! ### Zero objects of a full subcategory -/

section FullSubcategory

variable {C : Type*} [Category C] [HasZeroMorphisms C]

/-- **The inclusion of a full subcategory reflects zero objects.** The inclusion is faithful and
carries the identity of an object to the identity of its image, so an object whose image is zero
has `𝟙 = 0` and is itself zero. -/
theorem isZero_of_isZero_ι_obj (P : ObjectProperty C) (E : P.FullSubcategory)
    (h : IsZero (P.ι.obj E)) : IsZero E :=
  (IsZero.iff_id_eq_zero E).2 (P.fullyFaithfulι.map_injective (h.eq_of_src _ _))

end FullSubcategory

namespace Affine

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A]

/-! ### Koszul detection for the empty sequence -/

/-- **Koszul detection on `Spec A` for the empty sequence.** An object `M` of `D(𝒪_{Spec A})` with
quasi-coherent cohomology sheaves which receives no nonzero morphism from any shift of the Koszul
object of the empty sequence is zero.

This is `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_eq_zero` with its hypothesis
on the restriction to `U = D(f₁) ∪ … ∪ D(f_r)` *removed*, which is legitimate exactly because the
sequence is empty: that hypothesis enters the proof of the general statement only through the
`f_i`-power torsion of the cohomology modules of `N = RΓ(Spec A, M)`, and for `r = 0` there is no
`i` to produce it for. The rest of the argument is unchanged — the affine derived Spec–Γ
equivalence of [Stacks, Tag 06Z0] carries `M` to `N`, Hom-vanishing to Hom-vanishing against the
Koszul object of `D(A)`, and `Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_derivedKoszul_eq_zero`
concludes. -/
theorem isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_empty_eq_zero (f : Fin 0 → A)
    (M : DerivedCategory (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules)
    (hM : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf)) M)
    (h : ∀ (n : ℤ) (g : (Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.koszulObject f)⟦n⟧ ⟶ M), g = 0) :
    IsZero M := by
  let P := DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules)
    (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf)
  let Z : P.FullSubcategory := ⟨M, hM⟩
  let N := (derivedGlobalSectionsQuasicoherent (CommRingCat.of A)).obj Z
  have hcounit :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.isIso_derivedTildeQuasicoherentAdjunction_counit_app (CommRingCat.of A) Z
  let eZ : P.ι.obj ((derivedTilde (CommRingCat.of A)).obj N) ≅ Z.obj :=
    P.ι.mapIso (asIso ((derivedTildeQuasicoherentAdjunction (CommRingCat.of A)).counit.app Z))
  have hN : ∀ (n : ℤ) (g : (Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.derivedKoszul f)⟦n⟧ ⟶ N), g = 0 :=
    fun n g => AlgebraicGeometry.hom_eq_zero_of_hom_mapHomologicalComplex_eq_zero
      (CommRingCat.of A) ((Koszul.seqComplex f).extend ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat) N Z eZ n
      (h n) g
  have hNzero : IsZero N :=
    Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.isZero_of_forall_hom_derivedKoszul_eq_zero f N
      (fun i => i.elim0) hN
  have hZzero : IsZero Z :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.isZero_of_isZero_derivedGlobalSectionsQuasicoherent_obj
      (CommRingCat.of A) Z hNzero
  exact P.ι.map_isZero hZzero

/-! ### The Koszul object of the empty sequence is the structure sheaf -/

/-- The Koszul complex of the empty sequence is `A` in degree zero: in degree `0` it is the zeroth
exterior power `⋀⁰(A⁰) = A`, and in every positive degree it vanishes because a sequence of length
`0` has no exterior powers above degree `0`. -/
def seqComplexEmptyIso (f : Fin 0 → A) :
    Koszul.seqComplex f ≅
      (HomologicalComplex.single (ModuleCat.{u} A) (ComplexShape.down ℕ) 0).obj
        (ModuleCat.of A A) := by
  refine HomologicalComplex.Hom.isoOfComponents (fun n => ?_) ?_
  · by_cases hn : n = 0
    · subst hn
      exact (exteriorPower.zeroEquiv A (Fin 0 → A)).toModuleIso ≪≫
        (HomologicalComplex.singleObjXSelf _ _ _).symm
    · exact (Koszul.seqComplex_isZero_of_lt f n (by omega)).iso
        (HomologicalComplex.isZero_single_obj_X _ _ _ _ hn)
  · intro i j hij
    exact (Koszul.seqComplex_isZero_of_lt f i (by change j + 1 = i at hij; omega)).eq_of_src _ _

/-- **The Koszul object of the empty sequence is the structure sheaf in degree zero.** Sheafifying
the isomorphism `Stacks.Duality.Affine.seqComplexEmptyIso` termwise and localizing identifies
`Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.koszulObject f`, for `f` the empty sequence, with `𝒪_{Spec A}[0]`. -/
def koszulObjectEmptyIso (f : Fin 0 → A) :
    Stacks.Koszul.Truncation.koszulObject f ≅
      (DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules 0).obj
        ((tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A)).obj (ModuleCat.of A A)) :=
  DerivedCategory.Q.mapIso
    ((((tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A)).mapHomologicalComplex (ComplexShape.up ℤ)).mapIso
        ((ComplexShape.embeddingDownNat.extendFunctor (ModuleCat.{u} A)).mapIso
            (seqComplexEmptyIso f) ≪≫
          HomologicalComplex.extendSingleIso _ _ 0 0 rfl)) ≪≫
      (HomologicalComplex.singleMapHomologicalComplex (tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A))
        (ComplexShape.up ℤ) 0).app (ModuleCat.of A A))

/-! ### The affine case of [Stacks, Tag 09IS] -/

/-- **The affine case of [Stacks, Tag 09IS], in the ambient derived category.** Let `A` be a
commutative ring and let `M` be an object of `D(𝒪_{Spec A})` all of whose cohomology sheaves are
quasi-coherent. If every morphism `𝒪_{Spec A}[0]⟦n⟧ ⟶ M` vanishes, for every `n : ℤ`, then
`M = 0`.

This is the base case of the induction of [Stacks, Tag 09IS]: over an affine scheme the structure
sheaf is a generator of `D_QCoh(𝒪_X)`. It is Koszul detection for the empty sequence,
`Stacks.Duality.Affine.isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_empty_eq_zero`, transported along
`Stacks.Duality.Affine.koszulObjectEmptyIso`. -/
theorem isZero_of_forall_hom_structureSheaf_eq_zero
    (M : DerivedCategory (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules)
    (hM : (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB (A := (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules)
      (SheafOfModules.isQuasicoherent (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).ringCatSheaf)) M)
    (h : ∀ (n : ℤ) (g : ((DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules 0).obj
      ((tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A)).obj (ModuleCat.of A A)))⟦n⟧ ⟶ M), g = 0) :
    IsZero M := by
  refine isZero_of_forall_hom_koszulObject_empty_eq_zero (A := A) (fun i => i.elim0) M hM
    fun n g => ?_
  let e := (shiftFunctor (DerivedCategory (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules) n).mapIso
    (koszulObjectEmptyIso (A := A) fun i => i.elim0)
  rw [show g = e.hom ≫ e.inv ≫ g by rw [Iso.hom_inv_id_assoc], h n (e.inv ≫ g), comp_zero]

/-- The structure sheaf of an affine scheme, placed in degree zero, as an object of
`D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A})`: its cohomology sheaves are `(A)^~` in degree zero and zero elsewhere, and
`(A)^~` is quasi-coherent. -/
def structureSheafQuasiCoherent :
    (derivedQuasiCoherent.{u, u} (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))).FullSubcategory :=
  ⟨(DerivedCategory.singleFunctor (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)).Modules 0).obj
      ((tilde.functor (CommRingCat.of A)).obj (ModuleCat.of A A)),
    (DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryBPlus_singleFunctor_obj _
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentWeakSerre.isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre
        (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))) _ inferInstance).2⟩

/-- **The affine case of [Stacks, Tag 09IS].** The structure sheaf, placed in degree zero, is a
weak generator of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A})`: the only object of `D_QCoh(𝒪_{Spec A})` right orthogonal
to all of its shifts is the zero object.

This is `Stacks.Duality.Affine.isZero_of_forall_hom_structureSheaf_eq_zero` read inside the full
subcategory. Right orthogonality in the subcategory passes to the ambient derived category by
`CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_ι`, and the conclusion comes
back by `Stacks.Duality.isZero_of_isZero_ι_obj`.

It is the base case of the induction of [Stacks, Tag 09IS], in the shape the inductive step
`Stacks.Duality.OpenImmersion.isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_biprod_of_openImmersion` takes its
hypothesis `hP`. -/
theorem isWeakTriangulatedGenerator_structureSheaf :
    (ObjectProperty.singleton
      (structureSheafQuasiCoherent (A := A))).IsWeakTriangulatedGenerator := by
  have : (derivedQuasiCoherent.{u, u} (Spec (CommRingCat.of A))).IsStableUnderShift ℤ :=
    DerivedCategoryB.derivedCategoryB_isStableUnderShift _
      (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.QuasicoherentWeakSerre.isQuasicoherent_isWeakSerre
        (Spec (CommRingCat.of A)))
  exact fun E hE =>
    isZero_of_isZero_ι_obj _ E
      (isZero_of_forall_hom_structureSheaf_eq_zero E.obj E.property fun n g =>
        (Pretriangulated.rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_ofObj_iff _ _).1
          (rightOrthogonal_shiftClosure_singleton_ι _ hE) () n g)

end Affine

end Stacks.Duality

end
